  governs the versions that carry it.

  Reactive TUI holds code and data of other projects, each under its
  own license, which this license does not change. The file of each
  license is beside the part it covers:

    - crates/reactive-tui-crossterm (crossterm, MIT License);

    - crates/libghostty-vt and crates/libghostty-vt-sys (MIT License);

    - the parts of crates/reactive-tui-suprtui that come from OpenTUI
      (MIT License, LICENSE-OpenTUI);

    - src/accessibility/platform (Apache-2.0 or MIT, and the Chromium
      license);

    - src/terminal/pty/windows/runtime (MIT License, Microsoft);

    - src/graphics/fonts (the DejaVu fonts license).


